      "attack_scenario": "An attacker initiates Discord OAuth, obtains an authorization code, then injects it into a victim's browser as `/auth/callback?code=ATTACKER_CODE`; PKCE normally blocks this (the code is bound to the attacker's code_verifier, not the victim's), but if the victim has no active OAuth session or if PKCE is bypassed, the missing state check allows the callback to proceed and log the victim into the attacker's account (account takeover via OAuth login CSRF).",
      "checklist_id": "PROP-attendanceze-pre-002"
    },
    "text": "OAuth state parameter must match cookie-stored value before token exchange in STEM callback.",
    "assertion": "forall callback: tokenExchange(code) => req.query.state == req.cookies.oauth_state",
    "covers": "SG-006",
    "severity": "HIGH",
    "type": "pre-condition"
  }
}

